# MongoDB Environment Variables
# 
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
# ==================
# You can populate this file from your system environment variables:
#
# Option 1: Manual Setup
# ----------------------
# 1. Copy this file to mongodb_config/.env (in the mongodb_config subfolder)
# 2. Update the values below with your credentials
# 3. Ensure .env is listed in .gitignore (it already is)
#
# Option 2: Automatic Setup (Recommended)
# ----------------------------------------
# Run the appropriate setup script for your OS (both in the mongodb/ folder):
#   - Windows PowerShell: .\setup-env.ps1
#   - Linux/macOS Bash: ./setup-env.sh
# 
# These scripts will:
#   - Check for existing system environment variables
#   - Use system values if they exist, otherwise use defaults below
#   - Create the .env file in the mongodb_config/ subfolder
#   - The .env file is shared by docker-compose and the container
#
# Environment Variable Mapping:
# If you have system environment variables set, they will be used:
#   MONGO_ROOT_USER (or MONGODB_USER on some systems)
#   MONGO_ROOT_PASSWORD (or MONGODB_PASSWORD on some systems)
#   MONGO_DB_NAME (or MONGODB_DB_NAME on some systems)
#   MONGO_HOST (defaults to localhost)
#   MONGO_PORT (defaults to 27017)
#
# Default Values (used if environment variables are not set):

MONGO_ROOT_USER=admin
MONGO_ROOT_PASSWORD=changeme
MONGO_DB_NAME=myapp
MONGO_HOST=localhost
MONGO_PORT=27017
